1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,870
Singapore's Health Information Act was passed in January 2026.

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:11,360
It sets duties for new patient records, but not for the paper files clinics already hold.

3
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:20,360
It applies to healthcare licensees, retail pharmacies and approved users of the National Electronic Health Record.

4
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:27,790
The Ministry of Health lists phased deadlines in September 2027, September 2028 and March 2030.

5
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:30,630
The Act covers records going forward.

6
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:39,060
It does not require historical records or past consultation notes to be uploaded, so decades of paper case notes sit outside it.

7
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:47,690
Those files are still governed by the PDPA's retention and protection obligations, and by Ministry of Health record-keeping conditions.

8
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:53,120
Scanning turns legacy files into a searchable, access-controlled archive.

9
00:00:53,470 --> 00:01:01,040
For the records kept longest, archival microfilm to ISO 18901 adds a copy that no software change can lock away.

10
00:01:01,540 --> 00:01:06,610
Micrographics Data scans and indexes clinical and pharmacy records in Singapore.

11
00:01:06,960 --> 00:01:09,810
